Subject: [PATCH 5/6] port 07bfcded: serve: CPU replay of the Genesis request
 shapes through the 90f73293 parser and this one

A test only (serve/test_genesis_shapes_replay.py): the four Genesis request shapes and plausible model outputs for
them go through the production parser of 2026-10 and this tree's, whole and in deltas, tool arguments streamed and
not, recovery on and off, ended by a stop and by max_tokens; the request side (openai_to_messages, the rendered
prompt, the default-effort fill) is compared too.

Adaptations: 90f73293 is a fork-only commit, so its serve/frontend.py is vendored as
serve/fixtures/frontend_90f73293.py (unchanged but for a two-line header; not imported by the server) and the
test reads it from there, falling back to git. On v0.2.12 the parser changed on purpose (param_end options,
markdown code, the native tool parser, tool_call_recovery on by default upstream), so a difference this test
reports is a delta to review before a deploy, not by itself a bug; the docstring says so.

(cherry picked from commit 07bfcded2b69dd2ba8ce4b58258d7d5633a2849b)

